namespace trion:
    use formal
    use software

    section "The proof starts from the MMT form":
        The MMT form means the representation of a package in the MMT language.
        A proof obligation means a proposition that the MMT form of a package states about the package.
        The conversion means the transformation of a package into the MMT form of the package.
        Each MMT form has one or more proof obligations.

        [PROOF-OBLIGATIONS-WRITTEN]
        The trion processor shall write each proof obligation of a package into the MMT form of the package.

        [PROOF-FROM-MMT]
        The trioc command shall prove each proof obligation from the MMT form.

        [PROOF-ONE-TO-ONE]
        The trioc command shall report exactly one result for each proof obligation of the MMT form.

    section "What is not proved is stated as not proved":
        A bounded proof means a proof that holds within a bound.
        A bounded proposition means a proposition that names a bound.

        [PROOF-NOT-PROVED]
        If the trioc command does not prove a proof obligation, then the trioc command shall report the proof obligation as unproved.

        [PROOF-BOUNDED]
        The trioc command shall report each bounded proof as the proof of a bounded proposition.

    section "Certificates":
        A certificate means a document that an external proof checker checks.
        A certificate format means a format that an external proof checker reads.
        MoXI is a certificate format.
        Alethe is a certificate format.
        CPC is a certificate format.
        An external proof checker means a proof checker that is independent of the trion processor.

        [CERTIFICATE-ONLY-PROVED]
        The trioc command shall issue a certificate of a proof obligation only if the trioc command proves the proof obligation.

        [CERTIFICATE-INEXPRESSIBLE]
        If a certificate format cannot express a result, then the trioc command shall report the certificate format with an error or a warning.

        [CERTIFICATE-PROVED]
        If the verdict of a result is proved, then the trioc command shall issue a certificate of the result in each requested certificate format.

        [CERTIFICATE-EXTERNAL]
        An external proof checker shall check each certificate.

    section "What is trusted":
        The trusted base means the set of things that a person trusts for a result.
        The trusted base has one or more members.
        A language rule means a rule that expands a composite sentence or a rule that reads a simple sentence as a contract.

        No proof obligation states the conversion.
        An example demonstrates the conversion.

        [PROOF-NO-DISCRETION]
        The language rules shall determine the contracts of each package.

        [PROOF-CONVERSION-EXAMPLES]
        The trion processor shall pass each example of the language rules.

        [PROOF-TRUSTED-BASE]
        Each member of the trusted base shall be a language rule, the conversion, or an external proof checker.

    section "The metatheoretic proof":
        The metatheoretic proof means the proof about the language rules.

        [PROOF-RULES-KEEP-CONTRACTS]
        The metatheoretic proof shall establish that each expansion keeps the contracts of the composite sentence.

        [PROOF-NOT-SELF-VERIFICATION]
        The trion processor shall not accept a result about the specification of trion as the metatheoretic proof.

    section "The trioc command proves on its own":
        A query means a formula set that the trioc command decides for a result.
        An external program means a program outside the trioc command.
        The answer checker means the checker of the trioc command that shares no code with the solver of the trioc command.

        [PROVER-OWN]
        The trioc command shall not run an external program.

        [PROVER-CHECKED]
        If the answer checker rejects the answer of a query, then the trioc command shall report the result as unproved.

        [PROVER-OPEN]
        If the trioc command gives no answer to a query, then the trioc command shall report the result as unproved.
